-- title:
--   Zero normalized logarithmic rate of the local schedule length
-- statement:
--   For each natural $h$, let $L(h)$ be the length of the explicit local hash schedule on a block of $512h$ coordinates. This is the finite schedule generated by the prescribed greedy construction. Then
--   $$
--   \lim_{h\to\infty}\frac{\log L(h)}{2h\log2}=0.
--   $$
--   The logarithm is natural. Thus the local schedule length has zero exponential rate relative to the $2h$-bit local scale, which controls its contribution when local schedules are replicated across blocks.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/TrimScales.lean#L201-L223

